-- allium: 3
--
-- nixtune: a declarative network music player. A NixOS module
-- (services.nixtune.*) plus a PureScript (Halogen) page, built as a
-- public flake and consumed by the neoblade-config fleet as one input
-- and one row. A clean reimplementation of what moOde audio player
-- does, with none of moOde's code, none of its name, and none of its
-- runtime configuration machinery.
--
-- STATE OF THE WORLD, 2026-10-29. This revision exists so the work can
-- be handed off mid-stream. Facts first, design second.
--
--   Repositories (both on winsmuth, the workstation; neither pushed):
--     ~/git/nixtune             the public flake. flake.nix, .gitignore,
--                               nix/module/{default,hardware,mpd,library,
--                               ui,airplay,upnp}.nix, packages/upmpdcli.nix,
--                               packages/nixtune-web/{default.nix,spago.yaml,
--                               spago.lock,index.html,src/{Main,Mpd,Caps}.purs}.
--                               Its own flake.lock pins nixpkgs to
--                               6510408d147d8c5e6d76043e899e9251756f6a75,
--                               deliberately: see KnownIssue purescript below.
--     ~/neoblade-config         the fleet. Input `nixtune` =
--                               git+file:///home/bismuth/git/nixtune with
--                               nixpkgs following the fleet's. Adapter role
--                               modules/system/player.nix; rows `nixtune`
--                               (aarch64, Pi) and `nixtune-vm` (x86 QEMU) in
--                               targets.nix; facts in hosts/nixtune.nix and
--                               hosts/nixtune-vm.nix. The input is read from
--                               the checkout's committed tree, so a change in
--                               ~/git/nixtune needs `git add` there and
--                               `nix flake update nixtune` in the fleet.
--
--   Verified:
--     - Both fleet rows evaluate; `./build check` passes with only the
--       pre-existing fleet warnings plus two first-boot warnings for
--       nixtune (no secrets/nixtune.yaml yet: initialPassword from
--       base.nix, and services.nixtune.wifi.pskFile null from the module).
--     - `./build vm nixtune-vm`: mpd, nixtune-websocket and nginx active,
--       no failed units, no journal errors, capabilities.json served,
--       the page drove MPD end to end (GBH 89.7 queued and playing into
--       the null output). Streaming works; the first station URLs I
--       wrote were wrong and were replaced by GBH's published ones.
--     - packages.aarch64-linux.sd-image-nixtune builds.
--     - nixtune-web builds from spago.lock with nixpkgs' purescript
--       0.15.15 and esbuild (eighty fixed-output fetches, zero compiler
--       warnings); the page passed a 19-check headless browser test
--       against a protocol-faithful fake MPD.
--   Not yet done:
--     - The Pi has not been flashed or booted. Nothing about the DAC,
--       the overlay, AirPlay, wifi or the NFS mount has run on hardware.
--     - secrets/nixtune.yaml does not exist (it cannot until the Pi has
--       booted once and produced its host key).
--     - upmpdcli has never been built: packages/upmpdcli.nix carries
--       lib.fakeHash for all three tarballs. UPnP is declared off.
--     - LICENSE (AGPLv3) and README in ~/git/nixtune; the flake template
--       for adopters; the scope expansion below.
--
-- Design decisions that shape this spec:
--
--   1. The only source of configuration is the Nix declaration. No
--      settings database, no settings page, no daemon that rewrites
--      /etc or /boot. Changing a setting means a new generation, with
--      the previous one a reboot away.
--   2. Every optional capability is a sub-option with an enable flag
--      defaulting to false. A disabled one contributes no package, unit,
--      nginx location, firewall rule or UI element. Only MPD is
--      mandatory.
--   3. The page is a Halogen single page application that speaks the
--      MPD protocol itself over websockets bridged by websocat. There is
--      no backend code. The capability set is a JSON file Nix writes
--      into the static site at build time.
--   4. No over the air updates. Updates arrive only as new generations.
--   5. The root filesystem is NOT ephemeral yet, on purpose: the fleet's
--      wipe-on-boot has not been rehearsed on the Pi boot path (firmware,
--      U-Boot, extlinux, ext4 root from the generic SD image), and
--      oracle runs the same path without it. The module publishes what
--      it needs kept (services.nixtune.persistPaths = ["/var/lib/mpd"])
--      and the fleet adapter already maps that into homelab.persist, so
--      the manifest is correct from the first boot that has impermanence.
--   6. Two layers, one boundary. The public module knows nothing about
--      any fleet: the wifi passphrase is a runtime path to an
--      environment file, the library is one "host:/export" string, the
--      packages are built with the importing host's pkgs so no overlay
--      is needed. The fleet adapter (modules/system/player.nix, ~40
--      lines of config) maps homelab.nas.host plus roles.player.musicExport
--      to library.export, the sops secret to wifi.pskFile, and
--      persistPaths to homelab.persist.system. The machine, its boot
--      block, its secrets and its row live in the fleet; only the
--      mechanism is public. Keeping the two in sync is `nix flake update
--      nixtune` on the fleet's update branch, like every other input.
--   7. Maintenance is `nix flake update` on an update branch, CI
--      (`nix flake check`: the page build and an x86 rehearsal host),
--      merge to main. Nothing else.
--
-- Decisions taken 2026-10-26: AirPlay and UPnP as the first renderers;
-- wifi on the home 5 GHz SSID with the PSK as a sops secret; NFS
-- export /volume2/music from the Synology, nofail and automount; SD
-- card boot on oracle's path; a library browser in the first page; the
-- hardware profile from the DAC2 HD datasheet; DSP out of scope.
--
-- Decisions taken 2026-10-28 (scope for the public project, from a
-- questionnaire against moOde's feature list; everything was answered
-- yes, so the order below is the plan, and the three collisions are
-- recorded so nobody re-derives them):
--   Step 1  the Pi plays music over wifi from the NAS with AirPlay, as
--           built. Nothing else until this is true on hardware.
--   Step 2  the public release: flake template, HiFiBerry family and
--           generic USB DAC profiles; page gains tag browsing, cover
--           art, saved playlists, favorites (MPD stickers), three
--           read-only views (audio info, system status, service
--           health), a shipped curated station list plus runtime
--           station add kept in MPD playlists; ListenBrainz scrobbling.
--   Step 3  a real output arbiter, then renderers one at a time:
--           Spotify Connect, Squeezelite, Bluetooth sink, Roon Bridge
--           (unfree); MPD httpd output; several declared SSIDs; a
--           fallback access point.
--   Step 4  multiroom via snapcast, HDMI/touch kiosk, GPIO and rotary,
--           IR remote, USB and SMB sources, release images.
--   Collision A: "anyone who can flash a card" against "no runtime
--           configuration". A prebuilt image cannot know a stranger's
--           SSID or NAS. Resolution: the flake template is the public
--           entry point; images come in step 4 with a boot-partition
--           file for wifi and NAS only, documented as the one escape
--           hatch.
--   Collision B: five renderers against hook-script arbitration. The
--           before/after hooks work for one renderer against MPD; with
--           more they become pairwise agreements. An arbiter owning the
--           card is built before the second renderer.
--   Collision C: kiosk (a browser plus compositor on the Pi) and
--           Bluetooth sink (bluez plus bluealsa beside an ALSA-only
--           card) against "lightweight". Both are step 4, both off by
--           default, both the first to cut.
--
-- Deliberately outside this spec: the MPD protocol, the kernel's
-- device tree handling, nginx, and the renderer daemons' behaviour.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Given
------------------------------------------------------------

given {
    host: HostDeclaration
    player: Player
    output: OutputDevice
    module_repo: ProjectRepository
    fleet_repo: FleetConfig
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- External Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- neoblade-config: rows, roles, ./build, sops, attic. Governed by its
-- own spec (neoblade-config.allium). Here it is the consumer that
-- imports nixosModules.default and owns the machine.
external entity FleetConfig {
    repo_path: String
    input_url: String
    adapter_module: String
    build_command: String
}

-- A client on the network. Identity is by address only.
external entity Client {
    address: String
    on_lan: Boolean
    role: listener | operator | adopter
}

-- The Synology. Its NFS export allowlist decides whether the player's
-- address may mount; a missing entry presents as a timeout.
external entity Nas {
    address: String
    export: String
    allows: Set<String>
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

value SystemClosure {
    store_path: String
    flake_revision: String
}

value Track {
    uri: String
    title: String?
    artist: String?
    album: String?
    duration: Duration?
}

-- What nix/module/ui.nix writes to capabilities.json at build time.
value Capabilities {
    hostname: String
    profile: String
    output_kind: alsa | null_output
    card: String?
    mixer: String?
    modules: Set<ModuleKind>
    library: Boolean
    stations: List<RadioStation>
    websocket_path: String
    max_volume: Integer
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract PlayerModule {
    evaluate: (declaration: HostDeclaration) -> SystemClosure

    @invariant Purity
        -- Evaluation reads only the Nix declaration and pinned flake
        -- inputs. No network, no clock, no state from a previous
        -- generation. The page's dependencies are fixed-output fetches
        -- checked against spago.lock's integrity hashes, so evaluation
        -- never fetches; building does, once, with the network off
        -- afterwards.

    @invariant Determinism
        -- The same declaration and the same flake.lock produce the
        -- same closure on every machine.

    @invariant LazyModules
        -- A disabled sub-option contributes no package, no systemd
        -- unit, no nginx location, no firewall rule and no UI
        -- capability to the closure.

    @invariant NoRuntimeConfiguration
        -- Nothing in the closure writes to /etc, /boot or the Nix
        -- store at runtime.

    @invariant FleetAgnostic
        -- The module references no option outside the NixOS option
        -- tree it ships with nixpkgs and its own services.nixtune.*.
        -- homelab.* appears only in the fleet adapter.

    @guidance
        -- Options, as implemented:
        --   enable
        --   hardware.profile            "pi5-dac2hd" | "none"
        --   library.export              "host:/path" or null
        --   wifi.ssid, wifi.pskFile     pskFile is a runtime path to an
        --                               env file holding PSK=<passphrase>
        --   mpd.port (6600), mpd.exposeOnLan (false), mpd.maxVolume (100)
        --   radio.stations              [{name, url}]
        --   ui.enable (true), ui.package, ui.port (80)
        --   arbitration.resumeAfterRenderer (true)
        --   renderers.airplay.{enable,name}
        --   renderers.upnp.{enable,friendlyName,package}
        --   persistPaths                read-only, ["/var/lib/mpd"]
        --   output.{kind,card,device,mixer}   internal, from the profile
        -- Assertions: airplay needs output.kind = alsa; an ssid needs
        -- networking.networkmanager.enable (set by mkDefault when an
        -- ssid is declared). Warning: ssid set with pskFile null.
}

contract MpdBridge {
    status: () -> PlayerStatus
    command: (command: String) -> PlayerStatus
    capabilities: () -> Capabilities

    @invariant ReadOnlySystem
        -- The bridge speaks only the MPD protocol and serves the
        -- capability file baked into the closure. It cannot enable,
        -- disable or reconfigure any module.

    @invariant LanOnly
        -- nginx on 0.0.0.0:<ui.port>; websocat and MPD on loopback
        -- only (MPD on the LAN only with mpd.exposeOnLan). No
        -- authentication because there is no public exposure.

    @guidance
        -- websocat -t -E ws-l:127.0.0.1:8600 tcp:127.0.0.1:<mpd.port>
        -- as nixtune-websocket.service (DynamicUser, hardened), nginx
        -- location /ws proxying it with proxy_read_timeout 1h, static
        -- root = symlinkJoin of the page package and capabilities.json.
        -- The page opens TWO websockets: one for commands, whose
        -- replies are read against a queue of what was asked, and one
        -- parked in `idle player mixer playlist options database`.
        -- Nothing is polled.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum ModuleKind {
    mpd
    | airplay
    | upnp_renderer
    | spotify_connect
    | squeezelite
    | bluetooth
    | web_ui
}

enum NetworkKind { wired | wifi }

enum PlaybackState { playing | paused | stopped }

enum SourceKind { nfs | cifs | local | usb }

enum PersistKind {
    mpd_state_dir
    | host_keys
    | sops_age_key
}

enum ReleaseStep { pi_plays | public_release | arbiter_and_renderers | long_tail }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

entity HardwareProfile {
    name: String
    board: String
    dac_overlay: String?
    card: String?
    mixer_control: String?
    hardware_volume: Boolean
    needs_pi_kernel: Boolean
}

-- One player host, as declared. Fleet members declare the fleet; an
-- adopter's host has fleet = null.
entity HostDeclaration {
    hostname: String
    hardware: HardwareProfile
    network: NetworkKind
    ssid: String?
    psk_file: String?
    library_export: String?
    fleet: FleetConfig?

    modules: ModuleDeclaration with host = this
    enabled_modules: modules where enabled = true
    renderers: modules where kind in {airplay, upnp_renderer, spotify_connect, squeezelite, bluetooth}
    enabled_renderers: renderers where enabled = true

    music_sources: MusicSource with host = this
    radio_stations: RadioStation with host = this
    persisted_paths: PersistedPath with host = this
    generations: Generation with host = this
    secrets: SecretsFile? with host = this

    booted_generation: generations where status = booted
    capabilities: enabled_modules -> kind
    has_core: modules.any(m => m.kind = mpd and m.enabled)
    has_ui: modules.any(m => m.kind = web_ui and m.enabled)
    wifi_declared: ssid != null
    wifi_configured: ssid != null and psk_file != null

    invariant CoreIsMandatory {
        has_core
    }

    invariant OneBootedGeneration {
        booted_generation.count <= 1
    }

    invariant AirplayNeedsCard {
        enabled_renderers.any(r => r.kind = airplay) implies hardware.card != null
    }

    invariant PiProfileNeedsPiKernel {
        hardware.needs_pi_kernel implies hardware.dac_overlay != null
    }

    @guidance
        -- The fleet member: hostname nixtune, 192.168.8.222 reserved
        -- at the router, pi5-dac2hd, ssid PissiNet-5G, library export
        -- 192.168.8.110:/volume2/music, AirPlay on as "nixtune", UPnP
        -- off, stations GBH 89.7 (https://wgbh-live.streamguys1.com/wgbh)
        -- and CRB Classical 99.5 (.../classical-hi/), both from GBH's
        -- own help page. WBUR publishes no stream URL; the StreamGuys
        -- host is wbur-sc.streamguys1.com and the path is unverified.
        -- The rehearsal: hostname nixtune-vm, profile none, no
        -- library, no renderers, GBH only, page forwarded to
        -- localhost:8080, ssh on 2222.
}

entity ModuleDeclaration {
    host: HostDeclaration
    kind: ModuleKind
    enabled: Boolean
    state: inactive | active
    is_renderer: kind in {airplay, upnp_renderer, spotify_connect, squeezelite, bluetooth}

    invariant DisabledModulesAreInactive {
        not enabled implies state = inactive
    }
}

-- The fleet's sops file for the host. It cannot exist before the host
-- has booted once, because sops encrypts to the host's ssh key.
entity SecretsFile {
    host: HostDeclaration
    path: String
    has_user_password: Boolean
    has_wifi_psk: Boolean

    invariant WifiPskIsEnvFile {
        -- The wifi-psk entry holds `PSK=<passphrase>`, not a bare
        -- passphrase: NetworkManager's ensureProfiles substitutes
        -- $PSK from an environment file.
        has_wifi_psk implies true
    }
}

entity OutputDevice {
    host: HostDeclaration
    profile: HardwareProfile
    owner: ModuleDeclaration?
    volume: Integer

    invariant VolumeInRange {
        volume >= 0 and volume <= 100
    }

    invariant OwnerIsEnabled {
        owner != null implies owner.enabled
    }
}

entity Player {
    host: HostDeclaration
    state: PlaybackState
    current: Track?
    queue: List<Track>
    library_ready: Boolean
    last_error: String?
    sessions: Session with player = this
    open_sessions: sessions where status = open
}

value PlayerStatus {
    state: PlaybackState
    current: Track?
    volume: Integer?
    queue_length: Integer
    library_ready: Boolean
    capabilities: Set<ModuleKind>
}

entity Session {
    player: Player
    client: Client
    status: open | closed
    opened_at: Timestamp
}

entity MusicSource {
    host: HostDeclaration
    kind: SourceKind
    remote: String
    mount_point: String
    mounted: Boolean
    last_mount_attempt_at: Timestamp

    invariant FirstReleaseIsNfs {
        kind = nfs
    }

    @guidance
        -- fileSystems."/srv/music": nfs, ro nofail noatime noauto
        -- x-systemd.automount idle-timeout 600 mount-timeout 30s soft
        -- timeo=150 retrans=3. mpd.service after/wants
        -- srv-music.automount. music_directory is /srv/music and not
        -- under /var/lib/mpd, because the mpd module turns a music
        -- directory under its StateDirectory into a chown target that
        -- fails on a root-squashed export.
}

entity RadioStation {
    host: HostDeclaration
    name: String
    stream_url: String
    verified: Boolean
}

entity PersistedPath {
    host: HostDeclaration
    path: String
    kind: PersistKind
}

entity Generation {
    host: HostDeclaration
    closure: SystemClosure
    status: built | booted | previous | discarded
    built_at: Timestamp

    transitions status {
        built -> booted
        built -> discarded
        booted -> previous
        previous -> booted
        previous -> discarded
        terminal: discarded
    }
}

entity ProjectRepository {
    path: String
    public_url: String?
    main_revision: String
    nixpkgs_pin: String
    runs: UpdateRun with repo = this
    open_runs: runs where status in {opened, checked}
    issues: KnownIssue with repo = this

    invariant OneUpdateRunAtATime {
        open_runs.count <= 1
    }
}

entity UpdateRun {
    repo: ProjectRepository
    branch: String
    status: opened | checked | merged | abandoned
    ci_passed: Boolean
    lock_revision: String

    transitions status {
        opened -> checked
        opened -> abandoned
        checked -> merged
        checked -> abandoned
        terminal: merged, abandoned
    }
}

-- Things known to be wrong or unfinished, with the state they leave
-- the system in. Each one is closed by a commit, not by forgetting.
entity KnownIssue {
    repo: ProjectRepository
    name: String
    status: open | closed
    effect: String
    closes_when: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    mpd_port: Integer = 6600
    ui_port: Integer = 80
    websocket_port: Integer = 8600
    max_volume: Integer = 100
    nfs_mount_timeout: Duration = 30.seconds
    nfs_idle_timeout: Duration = 600.seconds
    resume_mpd_after_renderer: Boolean = true
    current_step: ReleaseStep = pi_plays
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Defaults
------------------------------------------------------------

default HardwareProfile pi5_dac2hd = {
    name: "Raspberry Pi 5 with HiFiBerry DAC2 HD",
    board: "raspberrypi-5",
    dac_overlay: "hifiberry-dacplushd",
    card: "sndrpihifiberry",
    mixer_control: "DAC",
    hardware_volume: true,
    needs_pi_kernel: true
}

default HardwareProfile none = {
    name: "No sound card (rehearsal)",
    board: "any",
    dac_overlay: null,
    card: null,
    mixer_control: null,
    hardware_volume: false,
    needs_pi_kernel: false
}

default FleetConfig neoblade = {
    repo_path: "/home/bismuth/neoblade-config",
    input_url: "git+file:///home/bismuth/git/nixtune",
    adapter_module: "modules/system/player.nix",
    build_command: "./build boot-native nixtune"
}

default ProjectRepository nixtune = {
    path: "/home/bismuth/git/nixtune",
    public_url: null,
    main_revision: "",
    nixpkgs_pin: "6510408d147d8c5e6d76043e899e9251756f6a75"
}

default KnownIssue upmpdcli_unbuilt = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "upmpdcli hashes are lib.fakeHash",
    status: open,
    effect: "renderers.upnp cannot be enabled; the fleet host declares it off",
    closes_when: "nix build ~/git/nixtune#upmpdcli has been through all three hash errors (libnpupnp 6.2.1, libupnpp 1.0.2, upmpdcli 1.9.4; versions unverified, lesbonscomptes.com was unreachable from the sandbox)"
}

default KnownIssue purescript_segfault = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "nixpkgs' prebuilt purs 0.15.15 segfaults in installPhase on nixos-unstable newer than the pin",
    status: open,
    effect: "the public repo's flake.lock is pinned to the fleet's nixpkgs revision; a plain nix flake update there reintroduces the crash until nixpkgs fixes it",
    closes_when: "a nixpkgs revision past the pin builds purescript, or the page build switches to a purs built from source"
}

default KnownIssue no_impermanence = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "ext4 root without wipe-on-boot",
    status: open,
    effect: "the fleet emits its ext4-root warning for nixtune as it does for oracle; persistPaths is mapped but inert",
    closes_when: "the rollback cycle has been rehearsed on a Pi and both Pi rows adopt it together"
}

default KnownIssue fleet_warnings = {
    repo: nixtune,
    name: "warnings at ./build check that are not nixtune's",
    status: open,
    effect: "/var/log bind-mount notes, scratch and winsmuth-vm secrets files, boot.zfs.forceImportRoot twice, oracle's catalogue entries, homebeacon test warnings; all pre-existing in the fleet",
    closes_when: "each is fixed in its own fleet commit; none blocks the player"
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Bring-up, in order ------------------------------------------------

rule OperatorBuildsImage {
    when: OperatorBuildsImage(operator)
    requires: host.fleet != null
    ensures:
        Generation.created(
            host: host,
            closure: { store_path: "", flake_revision: fleet_repo.input_url },
            status: built,
            built_at: now
        )

    @guidance
        -- winsmuth, in ~/neoblade-config:
        --   nix build .#packages.aarch64-linux.sd-image-nixtune
        -- The full attribute path: the image lives under the Pi's
        -- system, not the workstation's. Then, with the card in a
        -- reader and lsblk showing which device it is:
        --   sudo dd if=result/sd-image/*.img of=/dev/sdX bs=4M status=progress conv=fsync
        -- Done once already on 2026-10-29: the image builds.
}

rule FirstBootIsWired {
    when: HostBoots(generation)
    requires: generation.status = built
    requires: host.secrets = null
    ensures:
        generation.status = booted
        host.network = wired
        WarnedFirstBoot(host: host)

    @guidance
        -- ETHERNET CABLE IN. No secrets file exists, so: the account
        -- password is base.nix's initialPassword ("neoblade"), the
        -- module writes no wifi profile, and the machine answers on
        -- DHCP over the cable. The router reservation puts it at
        -- 192.168.8.222.
}

rule OperatorCreatesSecrets {
    when: OperatorCreatesSecrets(operator)
    requires: host.booted_generation.count = 1
    requires: host.secrets = null
    ensures:
        SecretsFile.created(host: host, path: "secrets/nixtune.yaml", has_user_password: true, has_wifi_psk: true)
        host.psk_file = "/run/secrets/wifi-psk"

    @guidance
        -- winsmuth:
        --   ssh bismuth@192.168.8.222 cat /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub \
        --     | nix shell nixpkgs#ssh-to-age --command ssh-to-age
        --   add the age key to .sops.yaml as nixtune_host with a
        --     creation rule for secrets/nixtune.yaml listing
        --     bismuth_winsmuth, bismuth_blade, nixtune_host
        --   env EDITOR=nano sops secrets/nixtune.yaml
        --     user-password: <mkpasswd -m yescrypt>
        --     wifi-psk: PSK=<passphrase>
        --   git add .sops.yaml secrets/nixtune.yaml
        --   ./build check            both nixtune warnings are gone
        -- The adapter sees the file exist and sets wifi.pskFile to the
        -- sops path; the module then writes the PissiNet-5G profile.
}

rule OperatorDeploysOverCable {
    when: OperatorDeploys(operator, revision)
    requires: host.secrets != null
    requires: host.network = wired
    ensures:
        Generation.created(host: host, closure: { store_path: "", flake_revision: revision }, status: built, built_at: now)
        WifiProfileWritten(host: host)

    @guidance
        -- winsmuth:
        --   ./build deploy-native nixtune      builds on the Pi, activates with test
        --   ssh bismuth@192.168.8.222 nmcli connection show --active
        --     must list PissiNet-5G beside the wired connection
        --   ./build boot-native nixtune
        -- Then unplug the cable, reboot, confirm 192.168.8.222 answers
        -- over wifi. The same cable-first order applies to every
        -- future PSK rotation (rotateManual in the adapter says so).
}

rule HostSwitchesToWifi {
    when: WifiProfileWritten(host)
    requires: host.wifi_configured
    ensures: host.network = wifi
}

rule HostBootsGeneration {
    when: HostBoots(generation)
    requires: generation.status = built
    requires: host.secrets != null
    let current = host.booted_generation
    ensures:
        for g in current:
            g.status = previous
        generation.status = booted
        CoreStarted(host: host)
}

rule OperatorRollsBack {
    when: OperatorRollsBack(operator, generation)
    requires: generation.status = previous
    let current = host.booted_generation
    ensures:
        for g in current:
            g.status = previous
        generation.status = booted

    @guidance
        -- The extlinux menu (configurationLimit 10) or
        -- `nixos-rebuild switch --rollback` on the Pi.
}

-- Hardware verification on the Pi --------------------------------------

rule OperatorVerifiesHardware {
    when: OperatorVerifies(operator)
    requires: host.booted_generation.count = 1
    ensures: HardwareVerified(host: host)

    @guidance
        -- On the Pi (ssh bismuth@192.168.8.222), each line with its
        -- expected answer:
        --   aplay -l                       a card named sndrpihifiberry
        --   amixer -c sndrpihifiberry scontrols       includes 'DAC'
        --   systemctl is-active mpd nixtune-websocket nginx shairport-sync
        --                                  four times active
        --   systemctl --failed             0 loaded units
        --   sudo -u mpd ls /srv/music      the library listing
        --   mpc status                     volume: n% and no ERROR line
        --   curl -s http://127.0.0.1/capabilities.json
        --                                  modules ["mpd","airplay"], library true
        -- From a phone: http://192.168.8.222/ plays GBH; AirPlay target
        -- "nixtune" appears and, while it plays, `mpc status` on the
        -- Pi shows [paused] if MPD was playing (the arbitration hook).
        -- If aplay shows no card, the overlay did not apply: check
        -- `cat /proc/device-tree/compatible` and the build log of
        -- hifiberry-dacplushd-bcm2712.dtbo.
}

-- Core and modules ------------------------------------------------------

rule CoreStartsOnBoot {
    when: CoreStarted(host)
    let core = ModuleDeclaration{host: host, kind: mpd}
    requires: exists core
    requires: core.enabled
    ensures:
        core.state = active
        output.owner = core
        player.state = stopped
        for m in host.enabled_modules where kind != mpd:
            m.state = active

    @guidance
        -- MPD: audio_output alsa on hw:CARD=sndrpihifiberry,DEV=0,
        -- mixer_type hardware on control DAC, no auto resample /
        -- channels / format, close_on_pause yes, replaygain off,
        -- restore_paused, auto_update. On profile none: the null
        -- output with a software mixer. alsactl persistence keeps the
        -- hardware level across reboots. The hifiberry overlay is the
        -- kernel's own dtbo with its compatible string rewritten to
        -- brcm,bcm2712, because nixpkgs applies an overlay only when
        -- it shares a compatible string with the DTB and the Pi 5 is
        -- not brcm,bcm2835.
}

-- Music sources and library -------------------------------------------

rule SourceMounts {
    when: SourceMountSucceeds(source)
    requires: source.mounted = false
    ensures:
        source.mounted = true
        LibraryRescanRequested(host: host)
}

rule SourceMountFails {
    when: SourceMountFails(source)
    requires: source.mounted = false
    ensures: source.last_mount_attempt_at = now

    @guidance
        -- With nofail and automount the failure is per access, not
        -- per boot: MPD starts, the library is empty, the next access
        -- retries. A NAS allowlist that omits 192.168.8.222 presents
        -- exactly like this.
}

rule LibraryRescans {
    when: LibraryRescanRequested(host)
    requires: host.music_sources.any(s => s.mounted)
    ensures:
        player.library_ready = true
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

-- Output arbitration (first release: one renderer) ----------------------

rule RendererAcquiresOutput {
    when: RendererStreamStarts(module)
    requires: module.enabled
    requires: module.is_renderer
    requires: module.state = active
    requires: output.owner = null or output.owner.kind = mpd
    ensures:
        if player.state = playing:
            player.state = paused
        output.owner = module
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- shairport-sync's run_this_before_play_begins: if `mpc status`
        -- says [playing], touch /run/shairport-sync/nixtune-paused-mpd
        -- and `mpc pause`. MPD's close_on_pause frees the card.
        -- upmpdcli needs no hook: it drives MPD, it does not open the
        -- card. This is the hook scheme Collision B retires before a
        -- second card-opening renderer is added.
}

rule RendererReleasesOutput {
    when: RendererStreamStops(module)
    requires: output.owner = module
    let core = ModuleDeclaration{host: host, kind: mpd}
    ensures:
        output.owner = core
        if config.resume_mpd_after_renderer and player.state = paused:
            player.state = playing
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- run_this_after_play_ends: if the marker exists, remove it
        -- and `mpc play` (only when resumeAfterRenderer).
}

-- Web interface and bridge --------------------------------------------

rule ListenerOpensSession {
    when: ListenerConnects(client)
    requires: client.on_lan
    requires: host.has_ui
    ensures:
        Session.created(player: player, client: client, status: open, opened_at: now)
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- The page fetches capabilities.json ONCE at load. A tab
        -- opened against an older generation keeps that generation's
        -- station list until reloaded; this cost an hour on
        -- 2026-10-28 and is worth a line in the README.
}

rule ListenerClosesSession {
    when: ListenerDisconnects(session)
    requires: session.status = open
    ensures: session.status = closed
}

rule ListenerSendsCommand {
    when: ListenerCommands(session, command)
    requires: session.status = open
    ensures:
        MpdProtocol.apply(player, command)
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- The page's own vocabulary: play/pause/stop/previous/next,
        -- random and repeat toggles, setvol clamped to maxVolume,
        -- clear/add/play for a station or a library path, play <pos>,
        -- delete <pos>, lsinfo <path> for browsing, load <playlist>.
        -- An MPD error line (ACK ...) is shown at the foot of the page
        -- and MPD keeps the last error in `status` until the next
        -- play or `clearerror`.
}

rule ListenerSetsVolume {
    when: ListenerSetsVolume(session, level)
    requires: session.status = open
    requires: level >= 0 and level <= config.max_volume
    ensures:
        output.volume = level
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)
}

rule StatusPushedToSessions {
    when: PlayerStatusChanged(player)
    for s in player.open_sessions:
        ensures: StatusDelivered(session: s, status: {
            state: player.state,
            current: player.current,
            volume: output.volume,
            queue_length: player.queue.count,
            library_ready: player.library_ready,
            capabilities: host.capabilities
        })

    @guidance
        -- The idle connection reports which subsystems changed; the
        -- page re-asks status and currentsong, and playlistinfo only
        -- when the playlist changed, lsinfo only when the database
        -- changed while the library view is open.
}

rule ListenerBrowsesLibrary {
    when: ListenerBrowses(session, path)
    requires: session.status = open
    ensures: LibraryListingDelivered(session: session, path: path)
}

rule ListenerPlaysRadio {
    when: ListenerSelectsStation(session, station)
    requires: session.status = open
    requires: station in host.radio_stations
    ensures:
        player.current = { uri: station.stream_url, title: station.name }
        player.state = playing
        PlayerStatusChanged(player: player)

    @guidance
        -- A station URL that redirects to an HTML page produces
        -- "avformat_open_input() failed: Invalid data found" in MPD.
        -- Verify a candidate from the player itself before declaring
        -- it: curl -sIL -m 10 <url> | grep -i -E '^(HTTP|content-type)'
        -- must end in 200 with an audio/* type.
}

-- Project maintenance -------------------------------------------------

rule MaintainerOpensUpdateRun {
    when: MaintainerRunsFlakeUpdate(maintainer)
    requires: module_repo.open_runs.count = 0
    ensures:
        UpdateRun.created(repo: module_repo, branch: "update", status: opened, ci_passed: false, lock_revision: "")

    @guidance
        -- In ~/git/nixtune. While KnownIssue purescript_segfault is
        -- open, an update that moves nixpkgs past the pin fails CI at
        -- the page build; the run is abandoned and the pin kept.
}

rule CiChecksUpdateRun {
    when: CiCompletes(run, passed)
    requires: run.status = opened
    ensures:
        run.status = checked
        run.ci_passed = passed

    @guidance
        -- `nix flake check`: checks.<system>.nixtune-web (the page) and
        -- checks.x86_64-linux.rehearsal (a hostless x86 system with
        -- profile none and one station). The devShell carries spago
        -- from purescript-overlay for editing the lock; consumers of
        -- the module never evaluate that input.
}

rule MaintainerMergesUpdateRun {
    when: MaintainerMerges(maintainer, run)
    requires: run.status = checked
    requires: run.ci_passed
    ensures:
        run.status = merged
        module_repo.main_revision = run.lock_revision
}

rule FleetFollowsModule {
    when: MaintainerMerges(maintainer, run)
    requires: run.ci_passed
    ensures: FleetInputBumped(fleet: fleet_repo, revision: run.lock_revision)

    @guidance
        -- In ~/neoblade-config: `nix flake update nixtune`, then
        -- `./build check`, then the fleet's own update-branch routine.
        -- Until the repo is pushed the input is the local checkout and
        -- reads its committed tree; after the push the URL becomes
        -- github:harryprayiv/nixtune and nothing else changes.
}

rule MaintainerClosesIssue {
    when: IssueFixed(issue, revision)
    requires: issue.status = open
    ensures: issue.status = closed
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant SingleOutputOwner {
    for d in OutputDevices:
        d.owner != null implies d.owner.state = active
}

invariant RenderersNeverOwnOutputWhileDisabled {
    for m in ModuleDeclarations:
        not m.enabled implies not (output.owner = m)
}

invariant WifiNeverWithoutSecretOnWifi {
    -- A host on wifi has a PSK file; a host without one is on the cable.
    for h in HostDeclarations:
        h.network = wifi implies h.wifi_configured
}

invariant PersistedPathsAreTheModulesList {
    for p in PersistedPaths where kind = mpd_state_dir:
        p.path = "/var/lib/mpd"
}

invariant MainIsAlwaysChecked {
    for r in UpdateRuns:
        r.status = merged implies r.ci_passed
}

invariant UpnpOffWhileUnbuilt {
    for h in HostDeclarations:
        upmpdcli_unbuilt.status = open implies not h.enabled_renderers.any(r => r.kind = upnp_renderer)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor Listener {
    identified_by: Client where on_lan = true
}

actor Operator {
    identified_by: Client where role = operator
}

actor Maintainer {
    identified_by: Client where role = operator
}

actor Adopter {
    identified_by: Client where role = adopter
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface PlayerUi {
    facing listener: Listener

    exposes:
        player.state
        player.current
        player.queue
        player.library_ready
        player.last_error
        output.volume
        host.hostname
        for m in host.enabled_modules:
            m.kind
        for s in host.radio_stations:
            s.name

    provides:
        ListenerConnects(listener)
        ListenerCommands(session, command)
        ListenerSetsVolume(session, level)
        ListenerSelectsStation(session, station)
        ListenerBrowses(session, path) when host.library_export != null
        ListenerDisconnects(session)

    contracts:
        demands MpdBridge

    @guarantee NoSettingsSurface
        -- No page changes system configuration.

    @guarantee DisabledModulesInvisible
        -- A renderer that is off has no badge; a host with no library
        -- has no Library tab; no stations means no Radio tab.

    @guidance
        -- Views: Now playing (title, artist/album line, progress,
        -- transport, random/repeat, volume slider to maxVolume), Queue
        -- (play by position, delete, clear), Library (breadcrumbs,
        -- add/play all, folders, playlists, files), Radio. Dark by
        -- default, light on prefers-color-scheme, phone-first.
}

surface FleetDeployment {
    facing operator: Operator

    exposes:
        host.hostname
        host.network
        host.secrets
        for g in host.generations:
            g.status
            g.closure.flake_revision
        for i in module_repo.issues where status = open:
            i.name
            i.effect

    provides:
        OperatorBuildsImage(operator)
        OperatorCreatesSecrets(operator) when host.booted_generation.count = 1 and host.secrets = null
        OperatorDeploys(operator, revision) when host.secrets != null
        OperatorVerifies(operator) when host.booted_generation.count = 1
        OperatorRollsBack(operator, generation) when host.generations.any(g => g.status = previous)

    contracts:
        demands PlayerModule

    @guarantee FleetShape
        -- One row in targets.nix (roles physical and player, nas.host,
        -- sdImage, the generic aarch64 sd-image profile in
        -- extraModules), one adapter module, two host files. The row
        -- is not special to ./build: deploy-native and boot-native
        -- treat it as they treat oracle.

    @guarantee TwoLayers
        -- hosts/nixtune.nix sets services.nixtune.* directly for the
        -- machine's facts and roles.player.musicExport for the fleet's
        -- one. Nothing under homelab.* is read by the public module.
}

surface CommunityFlake {
    facing adopter: Adopter

    exposes:
        module_repo.public_url
        module_repo.main_revision
        module_repo.nixpkgs_pin
        for i in module_repo.issues where status = open:
            i.name

    provides:
        OperatorDeploys(adopter, revision)

    contracts:
        demands PlayerModule

    @guarantee StandaloneUse
        -- Importing nixosModules.default, setting services.nixtune.*,
        -- and importing nixos-hardware's raspberry-pi-5 module for the
        -- Pi profile is the whole setup. No fleet, no sops, no attic.
        -- The flake template that makes this one command is step 2.

    @guarantee SharedLockfile
        -- Adopters build from the flake.lock main was checked with.

    @guidance
        -- AGPLv3 (LICENSE file still to be added). No moOde code, no
        -- moOde name.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred MpdProtocol.apply          -- see: https://mpd.readthedocs.io/en/latest/protocol.html
deferred DeviceTree.overlay         -- see: nixpkgs pkgs/os-specific/linux/device-tree/apply_overlays.py
deferred Renderer.airplay           -- see: shairport-sync documentation
deferred Renderer.upnp_renderer     -- see: upmpdcli documentation
deferred Websocket.bridge           -- see: websocat documentation
deferred Fleet.rows                 -- see: neoblade-config.allium

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Whether the Synology export /volume2/music lists 192.168.8.222 (or its subnet) and whether its squash setting lets the mpd user read; both show only on the Pi."
open question "Whether the rewritten hifiberry-dacplushd overlay binds on the Pi 5 kernel nixos-hardware ships (linux-rpi-6.18.50); aplay -l on first boot answers it."
open question "Whether WBUR's StreamGuys path is /wbur; verify from the player with curl before adding it."
open question "Whether the fallback access point (step 3) can coexist with the station connection on the Pi 5's single radio, or needs a second adapter."
